WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.152
Ever been asked what an explainer video actually is?

2
00:00:04.202 --> 00:00:07.031
It's a short video that explains one thing clearly.

3
00:00:07.081 --> 00:00:09.018
Here's the plain-English version.

4
00:00:09.518 --> 00:00:13.984
Every explainer answers one question and moves from problem to answer.

5
00:00:14.034 --> 00:00:16.967
Narration explains while visuals show.

6
00:00:17.017 --> 00:00:19.848
The goal is understanding, not advertising.

7
00:00:20.348 --> 00:00:23.595
Animation and live action take serious effort.

8
00:00:23.645 --> 00:00:30.017
Narrated slides do the same job, and many organisations already explain their biggest ideas in decks.

9
00:00:30.517 --> 00:00:35.773
A reliable shape is situation, problem, answer, proof, next step.

10
00:00:35.823 --> 00:00:40.604
Keep words and pictures matched, so when you say order page, viewers see it.

11
00:00:41.104 --> 00:00:43.783
Every extra minute should earn its place.

12
00:00:43.833 --> 00:00:49.322
Add captions and readable text, so people watching with the sound off can still follow along.

13
00:00:50.504 --> 00:00:52.834
Your speaker notes become the narration.

14
00:00:52.884 --> 00:00:58.117
On Pro, A.I. directs the video, so a plain deck lands like a produced explainer.

15
00:00:58.167 --> 00:01:01.404
Try Basic first at powerpoint2vid.com.

